1. Difference Between Docker and Kubernetes?
Short Answer
Docker is used to create and run containers, while Kubernetes is used to manage and orchestrate containers at scale.
Detailed Answer
Docker	Kubernetes
Containerization platform	Container orchestration platform
Creates images and containers	Manages containers
Runs on single machine	Runs across cluster of machines
Handles packaging	Handles deployment & scaling
No self-healing	Self-healing supported
No auto-scaling	Auto-scaling supported
Example
Suppose a banking application has:
 
Account Service

Payment Service

Customer Service

Notification Service
 
Docker:
 
Creates containers for each service
 
Kubernetes:
 
Deploys

Scales

Monitors

Restarts failed containers
 
Interview One-Liner
Docker packages applications; Kubernetes manages those containers in production.
